        "content": "<p><code>ring</code> doesn't know how to close reflexivity goals that are not equalities. How easy is this to fix?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: Try this:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [apply] ring_nf</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">  The `ring` tactic failed to close the goal. Use `ring_nf` to obtain a normal form.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">  Note that `ring` works primarily in *commutative* rings. If you have a noncommutative ring, abelian group or module, consider using `noncomm_ring`, `abel` or `module` instead.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: unsolved goals</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">x : ℝ</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ 0 ≤ 0 -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ring</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591379066,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777382142
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This does not seem to be in the scope of <code>ring</code> to me.</p>",
        "id": 591380599,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777382479
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The issue is that <code>ring</code> in such a case becomes noisy and suggests <code>ring_nf</code> instead</p>",
        "id": 591380893,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777382553
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A typical reason for me to reach this situation is by using <code>grw</code>, since <code>grw</code> doesn't try strengthening the goal from <code>&lt;=</code> to an equality after a generalised rewrite</p>",
        "id": 591386098,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777383664
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What’s wrong with <code>ring_nf; rfl</code>?</p>",
        "id": 591395250,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ledvinka",
        "timestamp": 1777385453
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe <code>ring</code> should be equivalent to <code>ring_nf; rfl</code>.</p>",
        "id": 591468174,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777404831
    }
